Write big-endian BMP decoder rows in the byte order consumed by imagelib.

The Userland graphics patches keep SurfaceFormat::OS_RGBA mapped to BGRA/BGRX
byte-layout surfaces so shared image buffers can be sent to WebRender.
nsBMPDecoder still builds each decoded row with gfxPackedPixelNoPreMultiply(),
which packs a host-order AARRGGBB uint32_t. On big-endian machines that lands
in memory as AA RR GG BB even though the SurfacePipe is consuming the row as
BGRA bytes.

Pack decoded BMP pixels explicitly as BGRA memory on big-endian builds. This
keeps ICO/BMP resources, including search-engine favicons, consistent with the
surface format already handed to the pipe.

Dependency: logically follows SPARC-01-cairo-surface-format.patch because it
matches the BGRA/BGRX image-buffer contract used by the Userland graphics
stack, but the code change itself is localized to the BMP decoder.

--- firefox-153.0/image/decoders/nsBMPDecoder.cpp
+++ firefox-153.0/image/decoders/nsBMPDecoder.cpp
@@ -170,9 +170,23 @@ }
 /// Sets the pixel data in aDecoded to the given values.
 /// @param aDecoded pointer to pixel to be set, will be incremented to point to
 /// the next pixel.
+#if defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) && __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__
+static uint32_t PackDecodedBGRAPixel(uint8_t aAlpha, uint8_t aRed,
+                                     uint8_t aGreen, uint8_t aBlue) {
+  return NativeEndian::swapFromLittleEndian((uint32_t(aAlpha) << 24) |
+                                            (uint32_t(aRed) << 16) |
+                                            (uint32_t(aGreen) << 8) |
+                                            uint32_t(aBlue));
+}
+#endif
+
 static void SetPixel(uint32_t*& aDecoded, uint8_t aRed, uint8_t aGreen,
                      uint8_t aBlue, uint8_t aAlpha = 0xFF) {
+#if defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) && __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__
+  *aDecoded++ = PackDecodedBGRAPixel(aAlpha, aRed, aGreen, aBlue);
+#else
   *aDecoded++ = gfxPackedPixelNoPreMultiply(aAlpha, aRed, aGreen, aBlue);
+#endif
 }
 
